	"_doc": "Building cell materials for the fine destruction grid (one byte per cell, 0 = empty, D-094). name: the BuildingVoxels palette key the cell draws with (a landmark_ material draws with its baked model's own colour, by class: wall greys, seat reds, pitch greens, anything else); strength: damage a cell takes before it breaks, relative to the other materials (uniform 1.0, today's uniform chunk strength, until the director tunes it); debris: the palette key its debris is coloured with; fixture: an attached, non-structural part (panes, mullions, signs) that holds on to the building where it touches a standing cell by a face, an edge or a corner (26 neighbours), where structural cells need a shared face (6 neighbours). Ids are stored in the grid: never renumber one.",
